.vercel

# secrets — .env.local holds SMTP credentials and the Buttondown API key.
# The example file documents the variable names and must stay committed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# `vercel link` appends its own `.vercel` and `.env*` rules here on every run.
# Both are already covered above — and a bare `.env*` placed after the
# `!.env.example` negation silently re-ignores the example file, so if the CLI
# adds them again, delete them rather than keeping the duplicates.
